Z||000000||DecadenceR||08-19-2001||01:26 AM||||As some of you know I recently installed a 40gig hard drive, and had a problem recognizing the entire drive space. Well, i got that fixrd by using FDISK to make a second partition on the drive. I used that 27 gig space as my MP3 and AVi storage space.<BR>Well, today, the entire partition is GONE. I have re-started several times, tried a system restore (using windows ME) ran EVERY Norton Utility, scan disk, the whole 9. And it's still no where to be found.<BR>Does ANYONE have ANY idea how i can fix this and hopefully get my 9 gigs of files back??? PLEASE ????||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||08-19-2001||01:54 AM||||How do you know it's gone? did you run fdisk and click on "show partition information"? If you did & its not there, I think partition magic or Partition commander may be able to get it back for you. That's the only way I know of. Sorry ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||08-19-2001||03:22 AM||||if you cant read your entire harddrive,<P>double check your drive cable in the computer case, mine was loose and windows was saying cant find partitions.  <P>I was playing with fdisk and lost one of my partition, nothing to inportant.  good thing<P>go to a pcmagazine site and download some fdisk programs, there are some that recover partitions.  But DONT PLAY WITH FDISK if you want to get the stuff back||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||08-19-2001||08:00 AM||||Be sure to look in fdisk first and make sure the partition is still there. <P>1. Create DOS partition or Logical DOS Drive<BR>2. Set active partition<BR>3. Delete partition or Logical DOS Drive<BR>4. Display partition information<P>Option 4<P>your cd could have taken over the drive letter. I have had that happen at work.<BR>I always set my CD drive letter to H now and don't have any problems adding or removing drives. All my programs work and see the drives and nothing gets bumped off.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DecadenceR||08-19-2001||12:04 PM||||I did look in FDISK, and it doesnt display it at all. Only shows the first partition that my OS is on. <BR>I am going to look on Download.com to try to find a program that does partition recovery, but if anyone else knows something, I'd be really happy to get any help possible.<BR>||||reg||1
