Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||08-20-2001||09:42 AM||||I know this sounds like closing the barn door after the horse has fled.<P> backup backup backup<P>if you have anything that is of value to you either:<P> 1. set up a second PC and make your own little 2 computer network, and use the 2nd ones HD to backup all your important files.<P> 2. use a CDR drive and put what you can on CDs - they are less than $0.20 each now in bulk - may be a problem for files larger than 720 Mbytes.<P> 3. for smaller stuff backup onto floppies - PKZIP is still usefull to get several megs onto a single floppy disk. <P>I came into work about 10 years ago and my PC was missing from my desk. Someone had broken into the company and stacked all the PCs on the platform of the loading dock, and they were just about to cart them all away when ADT showed up and scared them off. If my PC had been taken then all my work for the previous year would have been GONE!<P>  ever since then I always backup everything in a manner I can take home with me. My office building can burn to the ground, but the stuff I have invested my time into is safe.<P>  Hope you recover your files, and for everyone else this is a wakeup call - computers are not all that secure or reliable - if you have stuff that is valuable to you, back it up.||||reg||11
